<title>USA: Box Energy says voting shr ruling upheld.</title>
<headline>Box Energy says voting shr ruling upheld.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Box Energy Corp said on Friday a Delaware Supreme Court upheld a Chancery Court ruling which said Tom Box, one of several brothers, did not have voting control of Box Brothers Holding Co, which owns 57 percent of the Box Energy Class A common stock.</p>
<p>Tom Box, who was fired in August as chief executive officer and president of Box Energy, had contended that he owned the only voting share in Box Brothers Holding Co, a Box Energy spokesman said.</p>
<p>Tom Box was replaced as CEO by his older brother Don Box, in what people close to the situation called a family war over control of the company.</p>
</text>
